      "title": "Developing",
      "description": "The flanking arrows are pulling attention away from the center target more often than not, especially on incongruent trials — a common pattern that improves with practice.",
      "recommendations": [
        "Practice deliberately narrowing your focus to just the center position before glancing at the whole string",
        "Slow down very slightly on trials that feel like they 'flash by' — a rushed wrong answer costs more than a half-second of care",
        "Notice whether errors cluster on incongruent trials specifically — that's the interference effect, and it's normal early on"
      ],
      "order": 1
